## Can-Am X3 vs Maverick R at a glance

| | Maverick X3 | Maverick R |
|---|---|---|
| Who it suits | Has driven a buggy before | Already confident on sand |
| 30 minutes, two seat | AED 550 | AED 800 |
| 1 hour, two seat | AED 999 | AED 1500 |
| Four seat version | Yes | Yes, the X RS MAX |
| Minimum driver age | 14 | 14 |

The X3 Turbo RR sits between the two, on the X3 platform with more boost and firmer damping.

## How far apart the six Can-Am prices are

Every figure below is per buggy, and it already includes the helmet, the safety briefing, fuel, water and a lead guide.

| Can-Am model | Seats | 30 minutes | 1 hour | 2 hours |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Maverick X3 | 2 | AED 550 | AED 999 | AED 1750 |
| Maverick X3 | 4 | AED 600 | AED 999 | AED 1800 |
| X3 Turbo RR | 2 | AED 650 | AED 1200 | AED 1900 |
| X3 Turbo RR | 4 | AED 700 | AED 1300 | AED 2000 |
| Maverick R | 2 | AED 800 | AED 1500 | AED 2300 |
| Maverick R | 4 | AED 850 | AED 1500 | AED 2350 |

Two things stand out once it is laid out like this. The four seat **Maverick X3** costs exactly the same as the two seater for an hour, so a group of three or four should never split into two buggies to save money. And the Maverick R four seater at one hour is the same price as the two seater, which makes it the quickest way to put four people behind the most powerful platform we run.

## The three Can-Am platforms, and who each one is for

### Maverick X3: the step up

The [Can-Am Maverick X3 two seater](/dune-buggy-dubai/can-am-maverick-x3-2-seater/) is where most people meet the brand. It is turbocharged, it sits lower and wider than a Polaris RZR 1000, and the suspension soaks up a dune face that would unsettle a softer machine. It suits someone who has driven a buggy once before and wants more.

The [four seater](/dune-buggy-dubai/can-am-maverick-x3-4-seater/) is the one families and friend groups book, because one machine keeps everyone together on the route.

### X3 Turbo RR: more boost, stiffer damping

The RR badge means more boost and firmer damping. On paper it is a small change from the standard X3. In the sand it is a machine that punishes a lazy throttle and rewards a driver who commits to a line. We put experienced drivers only in the [X3 Turbo RR](/dune-buggy-dubai/can-am-x3-turbo-rr-2-seater/), and the guide decides at the base, not the booking form.

### Maverick R: the top of the fleet

The [Can-Am Maverick R](/dune-buggy-dubai/can-am-maverick-r-turbo/) is the fastest two seat machine we run. The four seat version, the Maverick R X RS MAX, is the top of the fleet for group bookings. Both are genuinely quick out of a dune bowl, and both are wasted on a 30-minute slot, because half of it goes on learning how much throttle the machine actually wants.

## When a Polaris is the better booking

This is the part a booking site will not tell you. For a driver who has never been in a buggy, a Can-Am is rarely the right first choice.

An hour in the Polaris RZR 1000 two seater costs AED 550. Thirty minutes in the Maverick X3 two seater also costs AED 550. A first-timer gets far more from the full hour: time to learn how the sand moves, time on the big red dunes once the guide is happy, and a photo stop at the end. On the Can-Am, the same driver spends most of a short slot finding the limits of a machine built for people who already know them.

We see it at the base most weeks. Someone books the most powerful machine in the fleet, drives it gently for twenty minutes, and wishes afterwards that they had booked the longer slot in the cheaper buggy. The [dune buggy price guide](/dune-buggy-dubai/price/) has all eleven buggies side by side if you want to compare the Polaris options properly.

## What happens before anyone drives a Can-Am

Every session starts the same way, whatever the machine.

1. Helmet fitting and the controls walkthrough, including the kill switch.
2. A warm-up on flat sand, where the guide watches throttle and steering.
3. The guided route into the Lahbab red dunes, with a lead guide in front and a sweep at the back.
4. A photo stop, then back to base.

The warm-up is where the Can-Am question gets settled. If the guide sees a driver who is not ready for an RR or a Maverick R, we move them to a machine that suits them on the same slot and adjust the price. Drivers must be fourteen or older, no licence is needed on our private desert routes, and passengers of any age can ride in a four seater.

## Booking a Can-Am with us

Message us on WhatsApp with the date, the group size and who is driving. We reply with availability, the total in AED and a pickup plan, usually within a few minutes. There is no deposit on standard slots, payment is cash, card or bank transfer on the spot at the base, and cancelling more than 24 hours before is free.

Driving yourself to the Al Awir base costs nothing and there is parking on site. Pickup and drop-off inside Dubai is an optional AED 300, and transfers from the outer emirates are quoted with the booking. We are open from 7am to 11pm every day.

We have run this base since 2020 and taken more than 17,000 guests into the dunes. The drivers who enjoy a Can-Am most are the ones who drove something gentler first, and the [full buggy fleet](/dune-buggy-dubai/) is sorted so you can see exactly where each one sits.
